mw2coop patch for maps/gulag_code.gsc (The Gulag, Modern Warfare 2, 64-bit Steam build)
Co-op logic lives in mw2coop/scripts/maps/_mw2coop_gulag.gsc.

1. Fly-in: player 2 rides the same helicopter on his own view controller (he would otherwise
   fall from the map's player start), at the same door as player 1, side by side as COD-MOD
   seats them: player 1's controller 20 units along tag_guy2, player 2's 10 units the other way.
@@@ subst spawn_player_heli
player_view_controller = get_player_view_controller( level.player_heli, "tag_guy2", ( 0, 0, -8 ) );
@@@ to
player_view_controller = get_player_view_controller( level.player_heli, "tag_guy2", maps\_mw2coop_gulag::door_offset( 1 ) );
@@@ end
@@@ replace
	level.player PlayerLinkToDelta( player_view_controller, "TAG_aim", viewPercentFrac, -35, 40, -35, 40, true );
@@@ with
	level.player PlayerLinkToDelta( player_view_controller, "TAG_aim", viewPercentFrac, -35, 40, -35, 40, true );
	maps\_mw2coop_gulag::partner_rides_heli();
@@@ end

2. The helicopter's turn around the gulag hides both players from enemies, not only player 1
   (maps\_mw2coop::players_ignoreme): both ride in it.
@@@ subst player_heli_rotates_properly_around_gulag
level.player.ignoreme = true;
@@@ to
maps\_mw2coop::players_ignoreme( true );
@@@ end
@@@ subst player_heli_rotates_properly_around_gulag
level.player.ignoreme = false;
@@@ to
maps\_mw2coop::players_ignoreme( false );
@@@ end

3. The riot shield watcher runs on each player (self, see maps/gulag.gsc): whoever carries the
   shield is the one enemies want and the nearest enemy aims well at; the armory's accuracy
   change for the whole level runs once, from player 1's watcher.
@@@ subst player_riotshield_threatbias
level.player
@@@ to
self
@@@ end
@@@ subst player_riotshield_threatbias
	thread modulate_player_attacker_accuracy_for_armory();
@@@ to
	if ( self == level.player )
		thread modulate_player_attacker_accuracy_for_armory();
@@@ end
@@@ subst player_riotshield_threatbias
			thread accurate_vs_nearest_baddie();
@@@ to
			self thread accurate_vs_nearest_baddie();
@@@ end
@@@ subst accurate_vs_nearest_baddie
level.player
@@@ to
self
@@@ end
